Build a single self-contained HTML file (vanilla JavaScript, Canvas 2D, no build step, no frameworks) called "Semiconductor Lab". It is an interactive teaching site with three pages: PN junction, Energy bands, and Diode lab. Reproduce every control, formula, label, and behavior below. Keep the visual design exactly as specified.

=====================================================
1. GLOBAL STRUCTURE
=====================================================

Header (sticky, top, full width):
- Left: brand text "Semiconductor Lab".
- Center/right: nav links "PN junction" (#junction), "Energy bands" (#bands), "Diode lab" (#diode). The active link has a 2px accent-colored underline (inset box-shadow at the bottom), no background.
- Right: a small pill button "Dark mode" / "Light mode" that toggles the theme.
- Header background uses the --hdr color with backdrop blur 8px and a 1px bottom border.

Routing: the page shows one section at a time based on location.hash. Listen to hashchange. Default to #junction. When a page is shown, re-measure and re-init its canvases. On window resize, re-measure the visible page's canvases (and re-seed particles on the PN and Bands pages).

Render loop: a single requestAnimationFrame loop. dt = min(0.05, elapsed seconds). Call frame(dt) on the currently visible page only.

Canvas helper: on each show/resize, set canvas.width/height to CSS size × devicePixelRatio and apply setTransform(dpr). Canvases are width 100% and fixed CSS heights (see sections below). Canvases stay transparent so the card or canvas-wrap background shows through.

Layout: a two-column grid on screens ≥960px (main column minmax(0,1fr), sidebar 340px, gap 20px). Below 960px, stack everything in one column. Each page: h1 title, a lede paragraph, then the layout.

Footer: a thin top border, muted small text: "Interactive teaching simulations · PN junction, energy bands, and diode characteristics."

=====================================================
2. THEME AND STYLE
=====================================================

Editorial, warm, serious-but-friendly. Think scientific journal paper.

Fonts:
- Headings and brand: serif stack "Iowan Old Style", "Palatino Linotype", Palatino, Georgia, serif.
- Body and buttons: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif. Base 14px / line-height 1.6.
- Numbers and formulas: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace.

Light theme (default, set on load):
--bg #f4efe6; --surface #fffdf8; --hdr rgba(244,239,230,.88); --fg #1c1917; --muted #78716c; --line #e5dccb; --soft #efe8da; --prose #44403c; --on #fffdf8; --accent #0f766e.
Carrier/diagram palette: electron/blue #0f766e; hole/red #c2410c; green #15803d; amber #b45309; sky #0e7490; violet #6d28d9.

Dark theme (html[data-theme="dark"]):
--bg #0f0d0b; --surface #191612; --hdr rgba(15,13,11,.88); --fg #f5efe6; --muted #a8a29e; --line #2c2722; --soft #211d19; --prose #d6cfc4; --on #0f0d0b; --accent #5eead4; color-scheme: dark.
Carrier palette: blue #5eead4; red #fb923c; green #86efac; amber #fbbf24; sky #67e8f9; violet #c4b5fd.

Implementation: a JS palette object for light and dark carrier colors. On toggle, set documentElement.dataset.theme and Object.assign the canvas color object (C) to the matching palette. The canvas color object is read at draw time, so every canvas drawing updates automatically. Fill surfaces (rounded boxes drawn on canvas) use C.surface, never a hard-coded white. Do not hard-code colors inside drawing functions except for glyph text on colored dots (white).

Body: background-color var(--bg) with a faint dot grid: background-image radial-gradient(var(--line) 1px, transparent 1px), background-size 22px 22px. min-height 100vh. Antialiased text.

Page heading: each h1 has a kicker drawn with ::before, 11px monospace, uppercase, letter-spacing .14em, accent color, margin-bottom 10px. Text per page:
- #page-junction: "01 — Junction"
- #page-bands: "02 — Energy bands"
- #page-diode: "03 — Diode"
h1: serif, 40px, line-height 1.08, letter-spacing -.015em, weight 500. On screens below 520px, 20px.
Lede: serif italic, 18px, muted, max-width 640px, margin-bottom 30px.

Cards (.card): border 1px var(--line), radius 6px, padding 20px, background var(--surface), shadow "0 1px 0 var(--line), 0 24px 48px -32px rgba(28,25,23,.45)". Variant .flush has padding 0 and overflow hidden, with a card header row (padding 12px 14px, bottom border).
Card header (.card-h): flex, space-between, wrap, 14px bottom margin.
Section label (.label): 11px, weight 600, uppercase, letter-spacing .12em, muted.
Canvas wrap (.canvas-wrap): border 1px var(--line), radius 6px, overflow hidden, background var(--soft).
Pill (.pill): monospace 12px, padding 2px 9px, pill radius, 1px border var(--line), muted text. Use accent or color override via inline style when showing a state.
Buttons (.btn): 1px var(--line) border, background var(--surface), text var(--fg), padding 6px 14px, radius 999px, 13px. Hover background var(--soft). Active: scale .96. Selected state (.on): background var(--accent), border accent, text var(--on). Small variant (.sm): padding 3px 9px, 12px, monospace.
Sliders: width 100%, accent-color var(--accent). Control rows (.ctrl): column flex, gap 8px, padding 12px 0, top border except the first. Control header (.ctrl-h): flex space-between, muted label, bold monospace value on the right. Scale row (.scale): 11px monospace labels below the slider (min, mid, max).
Checkboxes and labeled toggles: accent-colored checkbox with a label. Switch toggle (.switch): a 36×20 pill track; checked = accent fill; knob white with a shadow that slides 16px.
Stats (.stats): responsive grid, minmax(120px,1fr), gap 10px. Each .stat has 1px border, radius 10px, padding 10px 12px; a small muted label and a bold monospace value.
Formula box (.formula): monospace 12.5px, muted, padding 10px 12px, 1px border, radius 10px, background var(--soft). Variant .big: centered, 14px, inherits font, foreground color.
Prose (.prose): 13.5px, color var(--prose), paragraphs with 10px bottom margin, strong in foreground color weight 600.
Legend (.legend): flex-wrap, 12px muted text, 8px/16px gaps, padding 10px 14px, top border. Each legend swatch is a 10px circle, inline-block, 6px right margin.
Banner: hidden by default, shown with a flex row, padding 12px 14px, 1px border, radius 12px, background var(--soft).
Toast: 13px foreground text below a canvas, min-height 20px, auto-clears after 2.6 s.
Glassy aesthetics are NOT used on this site. Keep it editorial: flat surfaces, thin lines, soft shadows, one accent.

=====================================================
3. PAGE 1: PN JUNCTION (#junction)
=====================================================

Layout: main column (left) and sidebar (right).

Main column, top to bottom:
a) Mode buttons row: "1 · Joining", "2 · Unbiased", "3 · Forward +0.65 V", "4 · Reverse −3.0 V". The current mode button is highlighted (.on). Mode is derived from state: Joining if formation is active; Forward if V_D > 0.05; Reverse if V_D < −0.05; otherwise Unbiased.
b) Formation banner (visible only while joining is active): left side shows the stage title (bold) and description (muted note); middle is a progress bar (4px tall, accent fill, width = progress %); right has "Pause"/"Resume" and "Restart" small buttons.
c) Junction card (flush): header label "Physical junction · space charge" with two checkboxes "Spotlight minority carriers" (default off) and "Show recombination" (default on). Canvas height 400px. Legend: acceptor swatch (pink fill, red border) "Acceptor ion (−, fixed in P)"; donor swatch (light-blue fill, blue border) "Donor ion (+, fixed in N)"; hole swatch (red) "Hole"; electron swatch (blue) "Electron"; pill "W = x W₀" pushed right, updated each frame.
d) Barrier card: header label "Barrier potential and field" with pill "V_barrier = 0.70 V"; canvas-wrap containing a canvas 150px tall.

Sidebar, top to bottom:
e) Bias and parameters card: header label with a "Reset to 0 V" small button (sets mode Unbiased). Controls:
   - "Applied voltage V_D": header with "−0.05" small button, bold value (e.g. "+0.00 V"), "+0.02" small button. Range slider integer −100..100 (default 0). Mapping: slider s ≥ 0 → V = s/100 × 0.8; s < 0 → V = s/100 × 5. Scale labels: "−5.0 V", "0", "+0.80 V". The −0.05 and +0.02 buttons step V_D by those amounts, clamped to [−5, 0.8], and exit formation.
   - "Ideality factor n": bold value "1.00"; slider 1..2 step 0.05, default 1.
   - "Reverse saturation current I_s": value "10 nA"; slider 1..100 step 1, default 10.
   - "Temperature T": value "300 K · 25.85 mV"; slider 250..400 step 5, default 300.
f) Shockley equation card: header label with a state pill (text: "Joining", "Unbiased", "Forward bias", "Reverse bias", colored by state: joining amber, unbiased violet, forward green, reverse red). Big formula box: I_D = I_s (e^(V_D / nV_T) − 1) (with HTML sub/superscripts). Live formula box underneath: "I_D = 10 nA × (e^(0.00 V / 0.0259 V) − 1) = 0.00 nA" (update live). Stats row: "I_maj (diffusion)", "I_s (drift)", "Net I_D". Then a canvas-wrap with the I–V plot (220px tall).
g) Explanation card (prose): text changes by state, see section 3.3.

3.1 PHYSICS (exact):
- V_T = k·T / q, with k = 1.380649e−23, q = 1.60217663e−19. (At 300 K, 25.85 mV.)
- I_s in amps = IsnA × 1e−9.
- Effective applied voltage v = 0 while formation is active; otherwise v = V_D.
- ex = exp(min(35, v / (n · V_T))).
- I_maj = I_s · ex. Net I_D = I_s · (ex − 1).
- Built-in barrier V0 = 0.70 V. Barrier height bar = (formation ? V0 · progress : max(0.05, V0 − v)).
- Depletion width ratio wr: formation → progress; else if v ≥ 0 → max(0.24, sqrt(bar / V0)); else (reverse) → 1 + 1.15 · (|v| / 5).

3.2 CANVAS SCENE (junction canvas, width = page column, height 400):
Geometry: bx = max(45, w·0.09); bw = w − 2·bx; mx = bx + bw/2; dh = bw·0.135·wr (half-width of depletion region); dl = mx − dh; dr = mx + dh; re = bx + bw. Block top by = 78; block height bh = min(165, h·0.43); external wire y wy = by + bh + 78.
Draw order each frame:
1. Top current arrows (at y=22 for Is, y=38 for I_maj):
   - Is arrow amber, from (mx+15) leftward, length 45 (formation: 45·progress; forward: 35; reverse: 48). Label "I_s · minority drift" to the right, 11px semi-bold amber. Line width 2.5 when spotlight is on, else 1.5.
   - I_maj arrow green, from (mx−45) rightward, length: formation → 85·(1 − 0.55·progress); forward → min(115, 45 + (V/0.75)·70); reverse → max(8, 45·exp(2V)) (V negative); otherwise 45. Label "I_maj · diffusion" at its tip. Line width 2.5 when V>0.1 or formation, else 1.5.
   - Right-aligned text "I_D = I_maj − I_s" at (re, 32).
2. Field arrow: at y = by − 14, centered at mx, red, width 2.2, arrow from (mx+span) to (mx−span) where span = clamp(dh·0.85, 22, 85). Label "E · built-in field (N → P)" above in red 12px semi-bold. During formation with progress < 0.08, draw the text "No space-charge field yet (E = 0)" instead.
3. Blocks: P side (left of mx) tinted red at 7% alpha; N side (right of mx) tinted blue at 7%. Depletion region (dl to dr) filled light gray-blue (slate at 45% alpha) with dashed vertical edges, only if width > 3 px. A thin center line (mx) in a light gray. Block outline 1.5px gray-slate. Two gray contact bars on the left and right edges (7px wide, inset 18px top/bottom). Labels below the block at by+bh+22: "P region" (red, 13px semi-bold, centered over P side), "N region" (blue, centered over N side). If depletion width > 40 px, "depletion region" in muted 11px at +17px below the labels.
4. Ions (only if dh ≥ 8): columns at offsets 11 + 20k (k=0..) from mx, count = clamp(floor((dh−4)/20), 1..5), stopping when offset > dh − 6. Rows: 6 per column, spaced (bh−20)/6, starting at by+10. On the P side (left): acceptor circles (radius 7.5, pink fill #fecdd3, red stroke 1.4px, red "−" glyph). On the N side (right): donor circles (light-blue fill #bae6fd, blue stroke, blue "+" glyph).
5. Carriers (see 3.3). Majority holes (34) red circles r 4.5 with white "+". Majority electrons (34) blue circles r 4.5 with white "−". Minority electrons (4) blue circles, minority holes (4) red circles, each with an amber stroke (r 4.5 normally, r 6 with glow when spotlight on, and alpha 0.25 for the majority carriers when spotlight is on). Recombination flashes: amber rings that grow (radius +18/s) and fade (alpha −2.2/s).
6. External circuit:
   - Wires (gray-slate 1.6px) from each contact to a bottom wire at wy with loop corners at x = bx−28 (left) and re+28 (right). Battery sits on the bottom wire at mx.
   - Unbiased (V = 0 and not forming): white-filled box at the battery with label "Unbiased · 0 V".
   - Biased: four plate lines at dx = −14, −4, 6, 16 from mx, vertical half-heights 13 (long) or 7 (short). Forward: plates 0 and 2 are long (green), 1 and 3 short (sky). Reverse: plates 1 and 3 long (green), 0 and 2 short (sky). Polarity labels at the block contacts (+ green/− sky when forward; − red/+ green when reverse, 14px bold). Battery readout "V_D = +0.65 V" below the battery in monospace 11px.
   - Currents: forward (V > 0.1): green arrows on both wire loops labeled "I_D". Reverse (V < −0.1): an amber arrow labeled "I_s".

3.3 CARRIER MOTION (per frame):
- ts = sqrt(T / 300).
- Formation active (not paused) → diffusion flag if progress < 0.88. Non-formation: diffusion if V ≥ 0.25.
- Push (diffusion drift): non-formation and V > 0 → (V / 0.75)^1.6 · 2.6; formation active → (1 − progress) · 2.2; else 0.
- Majority holes: move by vx·ts + push (when diffusing); vertical bounce within block. When diffusing and x > dr + 15 + random·45, record a recombination flash (if enabled) and respawn at left edge (bx+8) at random height. Otherwise (not diffusing), clamp x to [bx+18 ... dl−8] with bounce. Min x = bx+8.
- Majority electrons: move by vx·ts − push when diffusing. Diffusing: when x < dl − 15 − random·45, flash and respawn at right edge (re−8). Non-diffusing: clamp to [dr+8 ... re−18] with bounce.
- Minority electrons: drift right at speed 2.2·ts inside the depletion zone (boost 1.6 when V < 0), else 0.65·ts. Respawn when x > dr + 45 at the left P region. Minority holes: drift left with the same rules, respawn when x < dl − 45 on the right N region.
- Vertical wrap for all carriers: bounce between the top and bottom of the block (inset 8 px for majority, 12 px for minority).

3.4 BARRIER PLOT (barrier canvas, height 150):
- Vertical guides at dl and dr (dashed light gray).
- Unbiased reference: dashed gray curve at the V0 level: flat at pY from bx to (mx − base), then bezier to (mx + base, uY), then flat to re. Where base = bw·0.135 and pY = h − 24, sc = h − 46, uY = pY − (0.70/2.8)·sc.
- Active curve: the same shape, using the current barrier height nY = pY − clamp(bar/2.8, 0.04, 1)·sc (flat at pY from bx to dl, bezier through (mx, pY) and (mx, nY) to (dr, nY), flat to re). Gradient stroke red → violet → blue, 2.5px. Fill the area below with blue at 6% alpha.
- "P" label at the left, red. Right-aligned label above the curve: "forming barrier", "reduced barrier", "increased barrier", or "equilibrium barrier V₀", followed by " · x.xx V".

3.5 I–V PLOT (Shockley canvas, height 220):
- Origin ox = w·0.46, oy = h·0.68. Right side (forward) spans 0 → 0.85 V over width rW = w − ox − 20; left side (reverse) spans 0 → −5 V over lW = ox − 24.
- Vertical: forward current maps to oy − min(1.05, I_mA / 25) × tH (tH = oy − 22). Reverse current maps down: oy + min(0.92, |I_nA| / 120) × bH (bH = h − oy − 18).
- Axes in gray; labels "+V_D (0.8 V)", "−V_D (−5 V)", "I_D (mA)", "−I_s (nA scale)".
- Curve in sky blue 2.2px: reverse from −5 to 0 (step 0.1), then forward 0 to 0.85 (step 0.01), using the current n, I_s, and V_T.
- Operating point dot (radius 5.5): green for forward, red for reverse, violet for unbiased/joining. Dashed guide lines from the dot to both axes.

3.6 STATE TEXT (explanation card, updated only when the state changes):
- Joining: "Instant of joining. Holes in P and electrons in N diffuse across the new boundary and recombine. Each electron that leaves N uncovers a fixed donor ion (+), and each hole that leaves P uncovers a fixed acceptor ion (−). These ions build a field E from N to P that slows diffusion."
- Unbiased (V_D = 0 V): "The uncovered ions form a barrier field E from N to P. It blocks nearly all majority carriers, while minority carriers are swept across as a small drift current I_s. Diffusion and drift cancel, so I_D = I_s(e⁰ − 1) = 0 A."
- Forward bias (V_D > 0): "The external source opposes the built-in field and lowers the barrier. The depletion region narrows, majority carriers diffuse easily, and I_D rises exponentially with voltage."
- Reverse bias (V_D < 0): "The external field adds to the barrier, so the depletion region widens. Diffusion falls to almost zero, leaving only the small reverse saturation current, I_D ≈ −I_s."
Use sub/superscript HTML for subscripts and exponents.

3.7 JOINING ANIMATION:
- Clicking "1 · Joining" resets progress to 0, sets V_D = 0, seeds particles, and shows the banner.
- Progress advances at 0.14 per second (scaled by dt) until 1, unless paused.
- Stage text by progress: < 0.30 "Stage 1 · Blocks joined" with "Majority carriers surge across the new boundary and recombine."; < 0.68 "Stage 2 · Ions uncovered" with "Electrons leaving N expose + donor ions; holes leaving P expose − acceptor ions."; otherwise "Stage 3 · Field builds" with "Accumulated ions create field E (N → P) that slows diffusion."; ≥ 0.99 "Equilibrium reached" with "The space-charge field balances diffusion. Net current is zero."
- Pause/Resume toggles the progress advance; Restart re-runs joining from 0.
- Dragging the voltage slider or step buttons, or choosing another mode, ends joining.

