5.1 MODEL (per material M with Vk, Is in nA, n):
Si: Vk 0.70, Is 10 nA. Ge: Vk 0.30, Is 250 nA. GaAs: Vk 1.20, Is 1 nA.
- Thermal: V_T = k·T_K/q with T_K = 273 + T °C, k = 1.38e−23, q = 1.6e−19.
- Knee vk(T) = max(0.15, Vk − (T − 27) · 0.0018).
- Ideal diode: if V_S > 0 → V_D = 0 and I_D = V_S / R (in mA × 1000). Else V_D = V_S, I_D = 0.
- Actual forward (V_D ≥ 0): I(mA) = max(0, 10·exp((V_D − vk)/(1.45·V_T)) − 10·exp(−vk/(1.45·V_T))).
- Actual reverse (V_D < 0): Is(T) = Is_nA × 1e−6 × 2^((T − 27)/12) in mA. I = −Is(T) × (1 − exp(V_D / V_T)). If |V_D| > V_BV − 0.35, add −18 × ((|V_D| − (V_BV − 0.15)) / 0.35)^2.6 (the Zener surge).
- Circuit operating point (solve V_D such that V_D + I(V_D)·R/1000 = V_S, with R = 500 Ω):
  - V_S ≥ 0: bisection on [0, min(V_S, vk + 0.45)], 28 iterations; if (mid + I(mid)·R/1000) < V_S then lo = mid, else hi = mid.
  - −V_BV < V_S < 0: V_D = V_S (no breakdown).
  - V_S ≤ −V_BV: breakdown; bisection on [V_S, −V_BV + 0.2], 28 iterations; if (mid + I(mid)·R/1000) > V_S then hi = mid, else lo = mid.
  - Store the final operating point and current I_D (mA).
- Plot: forward and reverse curve as described below.

5.2 CIRCUIT CANVAS (height 320):
- Package strip at top (inside a rounded box from y 8 to 64): diode package (rounded gray body at x = max(95, 0.22w), leads, cathode band) with labels "Anode (P)" (red, right-aligned) and "Cathode (N)" (blue). Symbol at x = min(w − 95, 0.78w): triangle pointing right in sky, bar in ink, with "+ Anode" and "Cathode −" labels. Skip the labels and captions when w < 480.
- Loop: rectangle with corners at (lx, bot), (lx, top), (rx, top), (rx, bot), where top = 100, bot = h − 34, lx = max(40, 0.10w), rx = w − lx, mx = w/2, my = (top + bot)/2.
- Source circle at (lx, my), radius 21, white fill, outline blue if V_S ≥ 0 else red, "+/−" glyph (top and bottom), label "V_S = +5.0 V" to its right.
- Resistor at (rx, my): white box with a zigzag, label "R = 500 Ω" (left of it) and "limits I_D" (green).
- Diode stage box at mx, width 230, height 82, top edge at y = top − 34, rounded radius 12, outline colored (red in breakdown, sky when forward, gray otherwise). Terminal leads from the box to ±58 px at the line y = top. Polarity glyphs inside the box corners. Content:
  - Ideal view (or tab 2): closed switch (thick sky line) "Short circuit · closed switch" with "V_D = 0 V · R_D = 0 Ω" when V_S > 0; open switch (red slanted blade drawn downward) "Open circuit · open switch" with "V_D = V_S · R_D = ∞ · I_D = 0" otherwise.
  - Actual: breakdown → red line plus a Zener symbol, "Reverse breakdown · V_BV = −20 V", "V_D = … · I_D = … mA". Forward above the knee → green line, diode symbol, "Conducting · knee ≈ x V", "V_D = … (ideal 0 V)". Forward below the knee → dashed amber line, "Sub-knee · below x V barrier", "I_D = … mA vs ideal … mA". Reverse → gray slanted blade, "Reverse bias · open switch equivalent", "I_s ≈ 0 mA (N nA leakage)".
- Loop current callout box centered at the bottom: "Loop current I_D = x.xx mA" (green) or "Loop current I_D ≈ 0.00 mA" (muted), red in breakdown.
- Animated current dots (16 dots evenly spaced along the loop): move at speed min(0.65, |I|·0.032) (sign follows current), drawn only when |I| > 0.05 or in breakdown. Color: red in breakdown, cyan in Ideal view, green otherwise. Dot radius 3.8.

5.3 I–V PLOT (height 340):
- Origin ox = 0.52w, oy = 0.60h. Forward: V 0 → 1.4 V maps to ox + (V/1.4) · rW (rW = w − ox − 24). Reverse: V 0 → −25 V maps to ox − (|V|/25) · lW (lW = ox − 28). Current: positive I maps to oy − min(1.05, I/20) · tH (tH = oy − 24). Negative I maps down: oy + off + min(0.95, |I|/20) · (bH − off), where off = 10 when Magnify is on (reverse region expands), bH = h − oy − 24.
- Gridlines at 5, 10, 15 mA (light gray). Axis lines gray.
